#: src/appendix-04-useful-development-tools.md:150
msgid "IDE Integration Using `rust-analyzer`"
msgstr "IDE 集成使用 `rust-analyzer`"

#: src/appendix-04-useful-development-tools.md:152
msgid ""
"To help with IDE integration, the Rust community recommends using [`rust-"
"analyzer`](https://rust-analyzer.github.io)<!-- ignore -->. This tool is a "
"set of compiler-centric utilities that speak [Language Server Protocol]"
"(http://langserver.org/)<!--\n"
"ignore -->, which is a specification for IDEs and programming languages to "
"communicate with each other. Different clients can use `rust-analyzer`, such "
"as [the Rust analyzer plug-in for Visual Studio Code](https://marketplace."
"visualstudio.com/items?itemName=rust-lang.rust-analyzer)."
msgstr ""
"为了帮助集成到IDE中，Rust社区建议使用(https://rust-analyzer.github.io)<!-- 忽"
"略 -->。该工具是一组以编译器为中心的实用工具，它们遵循(http://langserver."
"org/)<!-- 忽略 -->规范，这是一种用于指导IDE和编程语言之间通信的协议。不同的客"
"户端可以使用`rust-analyzer`，例如适用于Visual Studio Code的Rust分析器插件"
"(https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=rust-lang.rust-"
"analyzer)。"

#: src/appendix-04-useful-development-tools.md:159
msgid ""
"Visit the `rust-analyzer` project’s [home page](https://rust-analyzer.github."
"io)<!-- ignore --> for installation instructions, then install the language "
"server support in your particular IDE. Your IDE will gain capabilities such "
"as autocompletion, jump to definition, and inline errors."
msgstr ""
"请访问 `rust-analyzer` 项目的[主页](https://rust-analyzer.github.io)<!-- 忽"
"略 -->，以获取安装说明。然后，在您特定的集成开发环境中安装语言服务器支持。您"
"的集成开发环境将获得诸如自动完成、跳转到定义以及内联错误等功能。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:1
msgid "Appendix E: Editions"
msgstr "附录E：版本信息"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:3
msgid ""
"In Chapter 1, you saw that `cargo new` adds a bit of metadata to your _Cargo."
"toml_ file about an edition. This appendix talks about what that means!"
msgstr ""
"在第1章中，您了解到 ``cargo new`` 会在您的_Cargo.toml_文件中添加一些关于版本"
"的信息。本附录将详细解释这意味着什么！"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:6
msgid ""
"The Rust language and compiler have a six-week release cycle, meaning users "
"get a constant stream of new features. Other programming languages release "
"larger changes less often; Rust releases smaller updates more frequently. "
"After a while, all of these tiny changes add up. But from release to "
"release, it can be difficult to look back and say, “Wow, between Rust 1.10 "
"and Rust 1.31, Rust has changed a lot!”"
msgstr ""
"Rust语言和编译器有一个为期六周的发布周期，这意味着用户会不断获得新的功能。其"
"他编程语言则更频繁地发布重大更新；而Rust则更频繁地发布小规模的更新。随着时间"
"的推移，所有这些微小的变化最终会累积起来。但从一次发布到下一次发布之间，很难"
"回头感慨：“哇，从Rust 1.10到Rust 1.31，Rust确实发生了很大的变化！”"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:13
msgid ""
"Every three years or so, the Rust team produces a new Rust _edition_. Each "
"edition brings together the features that have landed into a clear package "
"with fully updated documentation and tooling. New editions ship as part of "
"the usual six-week release process."
msgstr ""
"大约每三年左右，Rust团队会推出一个新的Rust版本。每个版本都会将那些已经明确打"
"包的功能整合在一起，并提供完全更新的文档和工具支持。新版本的发布通常遵循六周"
"周期的常规发布流程。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:18
msgid "Editions serve different purposes for different people:"
msgstr "不同版本对不同的人来说有着不同的作用："

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:20
msgid ""
"For active Rust users, a new edition brings together incremental changes "
"into an easy-to-understand package."
msgstr "对于活跃的 Rust 用户，新版本将递增变化汇集到易于理解的软件包。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:22
msgid ""
"For non-users, a new edition signals that some major advancements have "
"landed, which might make Rust worth another look."
msgstr ""
"对于非使用者而言，新版本意味着一些重要的进展已经实现，这可能会让Rust变得值得"
"再次关注。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:24
msgid ""
"For those developing Rust, a new edition provides a rallying point for the "
"project as a whole."
msgstr "对于正在开发Rust的人来说，新版本为整个项目提供了一个新的发展方向。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:27
msgid ""
"At the time of this writing, four Rust editions are available: Rust 2015, "
"Rust 2018, Rust 2021, and Rust 2024. This book is written using Rust 2024 "
"edition idioms."
msgstr ""
"在撰写本文时，有四种Rust版本可供选择：Rust 2015、Rust 2018、Rust 2021和Rust "
"2024。本书采用Rust 2024版本的惯用法编写。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:31
msgid ""
"The `edition` key in _Cargo.toml_ indicates which edition the compiler "
"should use for your code. If the key doesn’t exist, Rust uses `2015` as the "
"edition value for backward compatibility reasons."
msgstr ""
"在_Cargo.toml_文件中，`edition`这个键表示编译器应该使用哪个版本来编译你的代"
"码。如果这个键不存在，出于向后兼容性的原因，Rust会使用`2015`作为该版本的默认"
"值。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:35
msgid ""
"Each project can opt in to an edition other than the default 2015 edition. "
"Editions can contain incompatible changes, such as including a new keyword "
"that conflicts with identifiers in code. However, unless you opt in to those "
"changes, your code will continue to compile even as you upgrade the Rust "
"compiler version you use."
msgstr ""
"每个项目都可以选择使用除默认版本2015之外的其他版本。这些版本可能包含不兼容的"
"更改，例如引入与代码中标识符冲突的新关键字。但是，除非您同意这些更改，否则即"
"使您升级了所使用的Rust编译器版本，您的代码仍然可以正常编译。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:41
msgid ""
"All Rust compiler versions support any edition that existed prior to that "
"compiler’s release, and they can link crates of any supported editions "
"together. Edition changes only affect the way the compiler initially parses "
"code. Therefore, if you’re using Rust 2015 and one of your dependencies uses "
"Rust 2018, your project will compile and be able to use that dependency. The "
"opposite situation, where your project uses Rust 2018 and a dependency uses "
"Rust 2015, works as well."
msgstr ""
"所有Rust编译器版本都支持在该编译器发布之前存在的任何版本，并且它们可以将任何"
"受支持的版本的库链接在一起。版本的变化只会影响编译器对代码的解析方式。因此，"
"如果你使用的是Rust 2015，而你的某个依赖项使用的是Rust 2018，那么你的项目仍然"
"可以编译并通过该依赖项运行。相反的情况，即你的项目使用Rust 2018，而一个依赖项"
"使用Rust 2015，同样也是可行的。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:49
msgid ""
"To be clear: Most features will be available on all editions. Developers "
"using any Rust edition will continue to see improvements as new stable "
"releases are made. However, in some cases, mainly when new keywords are "
"added, some new features might only be available in later editions. You will "
"need to switch editions if you want to take advantage of such features."
msgstr ""
"需要明确的是：大多数功能在所有版本中都可以使用。使用任何Rust版本的开发者将继"
"续享受到随着新稳定版本的发布而带来的改进。然而，在某些情况下，尤其是在添加了"
"新的关键字时，某些新功能可能仅适用于后续版本。如果您想利用这些功能，就需要切"
"换版本。"

#: src/appendix-05-editions.md:55
msgid ""
"For more details, see [_The Rust Edition Guide_](https://doc.rust-lang.org/"
"stable/edition-guide). This is a complete book that enumerates the "
"differences between editions and explains how to automatically upgrade your "
"code to a new edition via `cargo fix`."
msgstr ""
"更多详情，请参阅[_Rust版指南_](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/edition-"
"guide)。这是一本完整的书籍，详细介绍了各个版本之间的差异，并解释了如何通过"
"`cargo fix`自动将代码升级到新版本。"

