#: src/ch09-01-unrecoverable-errors-with-panic.md:170
msgid ""
"That’s a lot of output! The exact output you see might be different "
"depending on your operating system and Rust version. In order to get "
"backtraces with this information, debug symbols must be enabled. Debug "
"symbols are enabled by default when using `cargo build` or `cargo run` "
"without the `--release` flag, as we have here."
msgstr ""
"这确实会产生大量的输出！您看到的输出可能会因您的操作系统和Rust版本而有所不"
"同。为了获得包含这些信息的回溯信息，必须启用调试符号。当使用 `cargo build` "
"或 `cargo run` 且没有 `--release` 标志时，调试符号是默认启用的，就像我们在这"
"里看到的那样。"

#: src/ch09-01-unrecoverable-errors-with-panic.md:176
msgid ""
"In the output in Listing 9-2, line 6 of the backtrace points to the line in "
"our project that’s causing the problem: line 4 of _src/main.rs_. If we don’t "
"want our program to panic, we should start our investigation at the location "
"pointed to by the first line mentioning a file we wrote. In Listing 9-1, "
"where we deliberately wrote code that would panic, the way to fix the panic "
"is to not request an element beyond the range of the vector indexes. When "
"your code panics in the future, you’ll need to figure out what action the "
"code is taking with what values to cause the panic and what the code should "
"do instead."
msgstr ""
"在 Listing 9-2 的输出中，回溯路径的第 6 行指向了我们项目中导致问题的那一行代"
"码，即 _src/main.rs_ 的第 4 行。如果我们不希望程序出现 panic 情况，那么我们应"
"该从第一行所指向的位置开始调查，该位置所指向的文件是我们自己编写的。在 "
"Listing 9-1 中，我们故意编写了会导致 panic 的代码，解决 panic 的方法就是不要"
"请求超出向量索引范围的元素。当你的代码将来出现 panic 时，你需要弄清楚代码正在"
"使用哪些值来引发 panic，以及代码应该采取什么措施来避免这种情况。"

#: src/ch09-01-unrecoverable-errors-with-panic.md:185
msgid ""
"We’ll come back to `panic!` and when we should and should not use `panic!` "
"to handle error conditions in the [“To `panic!` or Not to `panic!`”](ch09-03-"
"to-panic-or-not-to-panic.html#to-panic-or-not-to-panic)<!-- ignore --> "
"section later in this chapter. Next, we’ll look at how to recover from an "
"error using `Result`."
msgstr ""
"我们将在本章后面的“是否应该转向 `panic!`”部分，再次讨论何时以及何不使用 "
"`panic!` (ch09-03-to-panic-or-not-to-panic.html#to-panic-or-not-to-panic)来处"
"理错误情况。接下来，我们将探讨如何利用 `Result` 来从错误中恢复。"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:1
msgid "Fearless Concurrency"
msgstr "无惧并发"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:3
msgid ""
"Handling concurrent programming safely and efficiently is another of Rust’s "
"major goals. _Concurrent programming_, in which different parts of a program "
"execute independently, and _parallel programming_, in which different parts "
"of a program execute at the same time, are becoming increasingly important "
"as more computers take advantage of their multiple processors. Historically, "
"programming in these contexts has been difficult and error-prone. Rust hopes "
"to change that."
msgstr ""
"安全且高效地处理并发编程是Rust的另一个重要目标。所谓“并发编程”，指的是程序的"
"不同部分能够独立执行；而“并行编程”则是指程序的不同部分同时执行。随着越来越多"
"的计算机利用其多个处理器，这两种编程方式变得越来越重要。历史上，在这些环境下"
"进行编程一直非常困难且容易出错。Rust希望改变这一现状。"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:11
msgid ""
"Initially, the Rust team thought that ensuring memory safety and preventing "
"concurrency problems were two separate challenges to be solved with "
"different methods. Over time, the team discovered that the ownership and "
"type systems are a powerful set of tools to help manage memory safety _and_ "
"concurrency problems! By leveraging ownership and type checking, many "
"concurrency errors are compile-time errors in Rust rather than runtime "
"errors. Therefore, rather than making you spend lots of time trying to "
"reproduce the exact circumstances under which a runtime concurrency bug "
"occurs, incorrect code will refuse to compile and present an error "
"explaining the problem. As a result, you can fix your code while you’re "
"working on it rather than potentially after it has been shipped to "
"production. We’ve nicknamed this aspect of Rust _fearless concurrency_. "
"Fearless concurrency allows you to write code that is free of subtle bugs "
"and is easy to refactor without introducing new bugs."
msgstr ""
"最初，Rust团队认为确保内存安全以及防止并发问题是两个需要分别用不同方法解决的"
"挑战。随着时间的推移，团队发现所有权系统和类型系统是一组非常强大的工具，可以"
"帮助管理内存安全和并发问题！通过利用所有权和类型检查，许多并发错误在Rust中都"
"是编译时出现的错误，而不是运行时出现的错误。因此，与其分别处理这些问题，不如"
"将两者结合起来使用。与其花费大量时间试图重现导致运行时并发错误的具体情况，不"
"如使用错误的代码会导致程序无法编译，并会显示错误信息来指出问题所在。因此，你"
"可以在编写代码的过程中就进行修复，而不是等到代码被部署到生产环境之后才发现问"
"题。我们将Rust的这一特性称为“无畏并发”。无畏并发让你能够编写没有这些问题的代"
"码。这些是隐蔽的缺陷，在重构时很容易修复，而不会引入新的问题。"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:25
msgid ""
"Note: For simplicity’s sake, we’ll refer to many of the problems as "
"_concurrent_ rather than being more precise by saying _concurrent and/or "
"parallel_. For this chapter, please mentally substitute _concurrent and/or "
"parallel_ whenever we use _concurrent_. In the next chapter, where the "
"distinction matters more, we’ll be more specific."
msgstr ""
"注意：为了简单起见，我们将许多问题称为“并发”，而不是使用更精确的说法“并发和/"
"或并行”。在本章中，当我们使用“并发”时，请将其替换为“并发和/或并行”。在下一章"
"中，当这种区别变得更加重要时，我们将使用更具体的术语。"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:31
msgid ""
"Many languages are dogmatic about the solutions they offer for handling "
"concurrent problems. For example, Erlang has elegant functionality for "
"message-passing concurrency but has only obscure ways to share state between "
"threads. Supporting only a subset of possible solutions is a reasonable "
"strategy for higher-level languages because a higher-level language promises "
"benefits from giving up some control to gain abstractions. However, lower-"
"level languages are expected to provide the solution with the best "
"performance in any given situation and have fewer abstractions over the "
"hardware. Therefore, Rust offers a variety of tools for modeling problems in "
"whatever way is appropriate for your situation and requirements."
msgstr ""
"许多语言对它们为解决并存问题提供的解决办法是教条主义的。 例如，Erlang具有消息"
"传递同义词的优雅功能，但在线程之间分享状态的方式却很模糊。 只支持一组可能的解"
"决办法是较高一级语文的合理战略，因为较高一级语文有可能放弃某种控制以获得抽象"
"的好处。 然而，较低级别的语文在任何特定情况下都将为解决方案提供最佳表现，而对"
"硬件的抽象程度则较低。 因此，Rust 提供各种工具，以适合您的情况和要求的方式模"
"拟问题。"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:42
msgid "Here are the topics we’ll cover in this chapter:"
msgstr "本章我们将讨论以下主题："

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:44
msgid "How to create threads to run multiple pieces of code at the same time"
msgstr "如何创建线程以同时运行多段代码"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:45
msgid ""
"_Message-passing_ concurrency, where channels send messages between threads"
msgstr "通过通道在线程之间传递消息的**消息传递**并发方式"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:46
msgid ""
"_Shared-state_ concurrency, where multiple threads have access to some piece "
"of data"
msgstr "多个线程可以访问某些数据的**共享状态**并发方式"

#: src/ch16-00-concurrency.md:48
msgid ""
"The `Sync` and `Send` traits, which extend Rust’s concurrency guarantees to "
"user-defined types as well as types provided by the standard library"
msgstr ""
"`Sync`和`Send`特性，它们扩展了Rust对用户定义类型以及标准库提供类型的并发保障"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:3
msgid ""
"<a id=\"extensible-concurrency-with-the-sync-and-send-traits\"></a> <a "
"id=\"extensible-concurrency-with-the-send-and-sync-traits\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"extensible-concurrency-with-the-sync-and-send-traits\"></a> <a "
"id=\"extensible-concurrency-with-the-send-and-sync-traits\"></a>"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:6
msgid "Extensible Concurrency with `Send` and `Sync`"
msgstr "通过`Send`和`Sync`实现可扩展的并发功能"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:8
msgid ""
"Interestingly, almost every concurrency feature we’ve talked about so far in "
"this chapter has been part of the standard library, not the language. Your "
"options for handling concurrency are not limited to the language or the "
"standard library; you can write your own concurrency features or use those "
"written by others."
msgstr ""
"有趣的是，我们在本章中讨论的几乎所有并发特性都已经是标准库的一部分，而不是语"
"言本身的一部分。处理并发的方式并不局限于语言或标准库；你可以自己编写并发功"
"能，或者使用其他人编写的功能。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:14
msgid ""
"However, among the key concurrency concepts that are embedded in the "
"language rather than the standard library are the `std::marker` traits "
"`Send` and `Sync`."
msgstr ""
"然而，在语言中嵌入的关键并发概念中，而非标准库中，有`std::marker`特性`Send`和"
"`Sync`。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:19
msgid ""
"<a id=\"allowing-transference-of-ownership-between-threads-with-send\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"allowing-transference-of-ownership-between-threads-with-send\"></a>"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:21
msgid "Transferring Ownership Between Threads"
msgstr "在线程之间转移所有权"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:23
msgid ""
"The `Send` marker trait indicates that ownership of values of the type "
"implementing `Send` can be transferred between threads. Almost every Rust "
"type implements `Send`, but there are some exceptions, including `Rc<T>`: "
"This cannot implement `Send` because if you cloned an `Rc<T>` value and "
"tried to transfer ownership of the clone to another thread, both threads "
"might update the reference count at the same time. For this reason, `Rc<T>` "
"is implemented for use in single-threaded situations where you don’t want to "
"pay the thread-safe performance penalty."
msgstr ""
"`Send`标记特性表明，实现`Send`的类型的值可以在线程之间转移所有权。几乎每个"
"Rust类型都实现了`Send`，但也有一些例外，包括`Rc<T>`：该类型无法实现`Send`，因"
"为如果你克隆了一个`Rc<T>`的值，并尝试将克隆后的所有权转移给另一个线程，那么两"
"个线程都可能进行更新操作。同时的引用计数。因此，`Rc<T>`被实现出来，用于单线程"
"环境下使用，这样就不必承受线程安全性能上的代价。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:32
msgid ""
"Therefore, Rust’s type system and trait bounds ensure that you can never "
"accidentally send an `Rc<T>` value across threads unsafely. When we tried to "
"do this in Listing 16-14, we got the error `` the trait `Send` is not "
"implemented for `Rc<Mutex<i32>>` ``. When we switched to `Arc<T>`, which "
"does implement `Send`, the code compiled."
msgstr ""
"因此，Rust的类型系统和特质约束确保你永远无法不小心地将`Rc<T>`值跨线程传输，从"
"而导致安全问题。在清单16-14中尝试这样做时，我们遇到了错误``，因为特质`Send`并"
"未为`Rc<Mutex<i32>>`实现``。当我们切换到`Arc<T>`时，该特质确实实现了`Send`，"
"于是代码就能够成功编译了。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:38
msgid ""
"Any type composed entirely of `Send` types is automatically marked as `Send` "
"as well. Almost all primitive types are `Send`, aside from raw pointers, "
"which we’ll discuss in Chapter 20."
msgstr ""
"任何完全由`Send`类型组成的类型，都会自动被标记为`Send`。几乎所有的原始类型都"
"是`Send`类型，除了原始指针，我们将在第20章中讨论这一点。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:44
msgid "<a id=\"allowing-access-from-multiple-threads-with-sync\"></a>"
msgstr "<a id=\"allowing-access-from-multiple-threads-with-sync\"></a>"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:46
msgid "Accessing from Multiple Threads"
msgstr "从多个线程访问"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:48
msgid ""
"The `Sync` marker trait indicates that it is safe for the type implementing "
"`Sync` to be referenced from multiple threads. In other words, any type `T` "
"implements `Sync` if `&T` (an immutable reference to `T`) implements `Send`, "
"meaning the reference can be sent safely to another thread. Similar to "
"`Send`, primitive types all implement `Sync`, and types composed entirely of "
"types that implement `Sync` also implement `Sync`."
msgstr ""
"`Sync`标记特性表明，实现`Sync`的类型可以从多个线程中安全地被引用。换句话说，"
"任何实现了`T`的类型都可以引用`Sync`，只要`&T`（对`T`的不可变引用）实现了"
"`Send`，那么这种引用就可以安全地传输到另一个线程。与`Send`类似，基本类型也都"
"实现了`Sync`，而那些完全由其他类型组成的类型则更是如此。实现 `Sync`，同时实"
"现 `Sync`。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:55
msgid ""
"The smart pointer `Rc<T>` also doesn’t implement `Sync` for the same reasons "
"that it doesn’t implement `Send`. The `RefCell<T>` type (which we talked "
"about in Chapter 15) and the family of related `Cell<T>` types don’t "
"implement `Sync`. The implementation of borrow checking that `RefCell<T>` "
"does at runtime is not thread-safe. The smart pointer `Mutex<T>` implements "
"`Sync` and can be used to share access with multiple threads, as you saw in "
"[“Shared Access to `Mutex<T>`”](ch16-03-shared-state.html#shared-access-to-"
"mutext)<!-- ignore -->."
msgstr ""
"智能指针`Rc<T>`也没有实现 `Sync` ，原因与它不实现 `Send` 一样。 `Refcell<T>` "
"类型(我们在第15章中谈到了这个类型)以及相关的 `cell<T>` 类都没有实现 "
"`Sync` 。 借方的实现检查了 \"Refcell<T>\" 在运行时不安全. 智能指针`Mutex<T>实"
"现了`Sync`，可以用来共享多个线程访问权限， 正如你在[“分享访问`Mutex<T>`”]"
"(ch16-03-shared-state.html#shared-access-to-mutext)<! - 忽略——。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:63
msgid "Implementing `Send` and `Sync` Manually Is Unsafe"
msgstr "手动实现`Send`和`Sync`是不安全的"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:65
msgid ""
"Because types composed entirely of other types that implement the `Send` and "
"`Sync` traits also automatically implement `Send` and `Sync`, we don’t have "
"to implement those traits manually. As marker traits, they don’t even have "
"any methods to implement. They’re just useful for enforcing invariants "
"related to concurrency."
msgstr ""
"因为完全由实现`Send`和`Sync`特性的其他类型组成的类型也会自动实现 `Send` 和 "
"`Sync`， 我们不必手动实现这些特性。 作为标记特征，它们甚至没有任何方法可以实"
"现。它们只是对强制执行与同义词相关的不变元素有用的。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:71
msgid ""
"Manually implementing these traits involves implementing unsafe Rust code. "
"We’ll talk about using unsafe Rust code in Chapter 20; for now, the "
"important information is that building new concurrent types not made up of "
"`Send` and `Sync` parts requires careful thought to uphold the safety "
"guarantees. [“The Rustonomicon”](../nomicon/index.html) has more information "
"about these guarantees and how to uphold them."
msgstr ""
"手动执行这些特性需要执行不安全的Rust 代码。 我们会在第20章中谈论使用不安全的"
"粉末代码； 目前的 重要的信息是，建造不是由`Send`和`Sync`零件组成的新的并行类"
"型需要认真思考，以维护安全保障。 [“Rustomicon”]（../nomicon/index.html）有更"
"多关于这些保障以及如何维护这些保障的信息。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:80
msgid ""
"This isn’t the last you’ll see of concurrency in this book: The next chapter "
"focuses on async programming, and the project in Chapter 21 will use the "
"concepts in this chapter in a more realistic situation than the smaller "
"examples discussed here."
msgstr ""
"这并非本书中关于并发性的最后内容：下一章将重点讨论异步编程，而第21章中的项目"
"将在实际场景中应用本章所介绍的概念，这些场景比这里讨论的较小示例要复杂得多。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:85
msgid ""
"As mentioned earlier, because very little of how Rust handles concurrency is "
"part of the language, many concurrency solutions are implemented as crates. "
"These evolve more quickly than the standard library, so be sure to search "
"online for the current, state-of-the-art crates to use in multithreaded "
"situations."
msgstr ""
"如前所述，由于Rust 如何同一种语言很少是语言的一部分，许多相同货币的解决方案都"
"作为箱子执行。 它们比标准库更快地进化，因此肯定要在线搜索当前最新的最先进的箱"
"子，以便在多线程环境中使用。"

#: src/ch16-04-extensible-concurrency-sync-and-send.md:91
msgid ""
"The Rust standard library provides channels for message passing and smart "
"pointer types, such as `Mutex<T>` and `Arc<T>`, that are safe to use in "
"concurrent contexts. The type system and the borrow checker ensure that the "
"code using these solutions won’t end up with data races or invalid "
"references. Once you get your code to compile, you can rest assured that it "
"will happily run on multiple threads without the kinds of hard-to-track-down "
"bugs common in other languages. Concurrent programming is no longer a "
"concept to be afraid of: Go forth and make your programs concurrent, "
"fearlessly!"
msgstr ""
"Rust 标准库为消息传递和智能指针类型提供通道， 例如`Mutex<T>`和`Arc<T>`，它们"
"可以安全地在并行环境中使用。 类型系统和借贷检查器确保使用这些解决方案的代码不"
"会最终导致数据竞赛或无效的引用. 一旦你得到你的代码进行编译， 你可以放心，它将"
"很高兴地在多个线程上运行，而不会出现其他语言常见的难以跟踪的 bug 。 同时编程"
"已不再是一个害怕的概念： 继续使您的程序并存，无所畏惧！"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:1
msgid "Shared-State Concurrency"
msgstr "共享状态并发"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:3
msgid ""
"Message passing is a fine way to handle concurrency, but it’s not the only "
"way. Another method would be for multiple threads to access the same shared "
"data. Consider this part of the slogan from the Go language documentation "
"again: “Do not communicate by sharing memory.”"
msgstr ""
"消息传递是一种很好的方式来处理同币种，但不是唯一的方式。 另一种方法是多个线程"
"访问相同的共享数据。 再次考虑Go 语言文档的这一部分口号：“不要分享内存。”"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:8
msgid ""
"What would communicating by sharing memory look like? In addition, why would "
"message-passing enthusiasts caution not to use memory sharing?"
msgstr ""
"分享记忆会有什么样子来沟通？此外，为什么信息传递爱好者会告诫不要使用内存共"
"享？"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:11
msgid ""
"In a way, channels in any programming language are similar to single "
"ownership because once you transfer a value down a channel, you should no "
"longer use that value. Shared-memory concurrency is like multiple ownership: "
"Multiple threads can access the same memory location at the same time. As "
"you saw in Chapter 15, where smart pointers made multiple ownership "
"possible, multiple ownership can add complexity because these different "
"owners need managing. Rust’s type system and ownership rules greatly assist "
"in getting this management correct. For an example, let’s look at mutexes, "
"one of the more common concurrency primitives for shared memory."
msgstr ""
"从某种意义上讲，任何编程语言中的频道都类似于单个所有权，因为一旦您转移了一个"
"通道的值。 您不应再使用该值。 共享内存同义类似于多个所有者：多个线程可以同时"
"访问相同的内存位置。 正如你在第15章中所看到的那样，智能指针使得多个所有权成为"
"可能，多个所有权可以增加复杂性，因为这些不同的所有者需要管理。 俄罗斯的类型系"
"统和所有权规则极大地有助于使管理正确无误。 例如，让我们看一下mutexes，一个更"
"常见的内存首字母。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:23
msgid ""
"<a id=\"using-mutexes-to-allow-access-to-data-from-one-thread-at-a-time\"></"
"a>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"using-mutexes-to-allow-access-to-data-from-one-thread-at-a-time\"></"
"a>"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:25
msgid "Controlling Access with Mutexes"
msgstr "使用互斥锁控制访问"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:27
msgid ""
"_Mutex_ is an abbreviation for _mutual exclusion_, as in a mutex allows only "
"one thread to access some data at any given time. To access the data in a "
"mutex, a thread must first signal that it wants access by asking to acquire "
"the mutex’s lock. The _lock_ is a data structure that is part of the mutex "
"that keeps track of who currently has exclusive access to the data. "
"Therefore, the mutex is described as _guarding_ the data it holds via the "
"locking system."
msgstr ""
"_Mutex_是_互斥_的缩写，意味着在任何给定时间，只有一个线程可以访问某些数据。要"
"访问mutex中的数据，线程必须先通过请求获取mutex的锁来表明它希望访问这些数据。_"
"锁_是一种数据结构，它是mutex的一部分，用于记录当前谁拥有对数据的独占访问权。"
"因此，mutex通过锁定系统来“保护”其所持有的数据。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:34
msgid ""
"Mutexes have a reputation for being difficult to use because you have to "
"remember two rules:"
msgstr "由于您必须记住两条规则，因此Musexes 因难以使用而信誉积分："

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:37
msgid "You must attempt to acquire the lock before using the data."
msgstr "您必须先尝试获取锁定才能使用数据。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:38
msgid ""
"When you’re done with the data that the mutex guards, you must unlock the "
"data so that other threads can acquire the lock."
msgstr ""
"当你使用mutex护卫的数据完成时，你必须解锁数据，以便其他线程能够获取锁定。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:41
msgid ""
"For a real-world metaphor for a mutex, imagine a panel discussion at a "
"conference with only one microphone. Before a panelist can speak, they have "
"to ask or signal that they want to use the microphone. When they get the "
"microphone, they can talk for as long as they want to and then hand the "
"microphone to the next panelist who requests to speak. If a panelist forgets "
"to hand the microphone off when they’re finished with it, no one else is "
"able to speak. If management of the shared microphone goes wrong, the panel "
"won’t work as planned!"
msgstr ""
"为了更好地理解互斥锁的工作原理，我们可以想象一个会议上的小组讨论场景。在这个"
"场景中，只有一个麦克风可供使用。在一位小组成员发言之前，他们必须先请求或示意"
"其他小组成员可以使用麦克风。当他们拿到麦克风后，就可以随心所欲地发言，然后将"
"其交给下一位想要发言的小组成员。如果某位小组成员在发言结束后忘记将麦克风交"
"还，那么其他成员就无法发言了。如果共享麦克风的管理不当，整个讨论就会无法按计"
"划进行！"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:50
msgid ""
"Management of mutexes can be incredibly tricky to get right, which is why so "
"many people are enthusiastic about channels. However, thanks to Rust’s type "
"system and ownership rules, you can’t get locking and unlocking wrong."
msgstr ""
"互斥体的管理非常难以掌握，这就是为什么很多人对通道感到兴奋。不过，得益于Rust"
"的类型系统和所有权规则，锁定与解锁的操作根本不会出错。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:54
msgid "The API of `Mutex<T>`"
msgstr "`Mutex<T>` 的 API"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:56
msgid ""
"As an example of how to use a mutex, let’s start by using a mutex in a "
"single-threaded context, as shown in Listing 16-12."
msgstr ""
"作为使用互斥锁的一个示例，我们先来看一下在单线程环境中如何使用互斥锁，如清单 "
"16-12 所示。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:72
msgid "\"m = {m:?}\""
msgstr "\"m = {m:?}\""

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:78
msgid ""
"As with many types, we create a `Mutex<T>` using the associated function "
"`new`. To access the data inside the mutex, we use the `lock` method to "
"acquire the lock. This call will block the current thread so that it can’t "
"do any work until it’s our turn to have the lock."
msgstr ""
"和许多类型一样，我们使用相关函数`new`创建一个 `Mutex<T>`。 为了访问mutex内部"
"的数据，我们使用 `lock` 方法获取锁定。 此通话将阻止当前的线程，以便在我们转向"
"锁定之前它无法完成任何工作。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:83
msgid ""
"The call to `lock` would fail if another thread holding the lock panicked. "
"In that case, no one would ever be able to get the lock, so we’ve chosen to "
"`unwrap` and have this thread panic if we’re in that situation."
msgstr ""
"如果持有锁定的另一个线程出现恐慌，调用`lock`将失败。 在这种情况下，任何人都无"
"法得到锁定， 所以，如果我们处于这种局面，我们选择`解除包裹'并有这个线程恐慌。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:87
msgid ""
"After we’ve acquired the lock, we can treat the return value, named `num` in "
"this case, as a mutable reference to the data inside. The type system "
"ensures that we acquire a lock before using the value in `m`. The type of "
"`m` is `Mutex<i32>`, not `i32`, so we _must_ call `lock` to be able to use "
"the `i32` value. We can’t forget; the type system won’t let us access the "
"inner `i32` otherwise."
msgstr ""
"当我们获得锁定后，我们可以将这个名为`num`的退货值作为可变的内在数据引用。 类"
"型系统确保我们在使用\"m\"中的值之前获得一个锁。 `m`的类型是 `Mutex<i32>`，而"
"不是 `i32`，所以我们必须调用`lock` 才能使用 `i32` 值。 我们不能忘记；这种类型"
"的系统不会让我们以其他方式访问内部的 i32。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:94
msgid ""
"The call to `lock` returns a type called `MutexGuard`, wrapped in a "
"`LockResult` that we handled with the call to `unwrap`. The `MutexGuard` "
"type implements `Deref` to point at our inner data; the type also has a "
"`Drop` implementation that releases the lock automatically when a "
"`MutexGuard` goes out of scope, which happens at the end of the inner scope. "
"As a result, we don’t risk forgetting to release the lock and blocking the "
"mutex from being used by other threads because the lock release happens "
"automatically."
msgstr ""
"调用`lock`返回一个叫`MutexGuard`的类型，包装在一个 `LockResult` 中，我们用调"
"用`unwrawra`来电来处理这个类型。 `MutexGuard`型号实现`Deref`，指向我们的内部"
"数据； 类型还有一个 `Drop` 实现，在一个 `MutexGuard` 超出范围时自动释放锁， "
"内部范围末尾发生这种情况。 结果， 我们不会忘记解锁锁并阻止mutex 被其他线程使"
"用，因为锁定会自动释放。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:102
msgid ""
"After dropping the lock, we can print the mutex value and see that we were "
"able to change the inner `i32` to `6`."
msgstr ""
"在释放锁之后，我们可以打印出互斥量的值，从而看到我们成功地将内部的 `i32` 改为"
"了 `6`。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:107
msgid "<a id=\"sharing-a-mutext-between-multiple-threads\"></a>"
msgstr "<a id=\"sharing-a-mutext-between-multiple-threads\"></a>"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:109
msgid "Shared Access to `Mutex<T>`"
msgstr "共享访问 `Mutex<T>`"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:111
msgid ""
"Now let’s try to share a value between multiple threads using `Mutex<T>`. "
"We’ll spin up 10 threads and have them each increment a counter value by 1, "
"so the counter goes from 0 to 10. The example in Listing 16-13 will have a "
"compiler error, and we’ll use that error to learn more about using "
"`Mutex<T>` and how Rust helps us use it correctly."
msgstr ""
"现在让我们尝试使用`Mutex<T>`在多个线程之间分享一个值。 我们将会增加10条线程，"
"并使它们每次递增一个计数器1，因此计数器会从0增加到10。 上架16-13中的示例将有"
"一个编译器错误， 并且我们将使用这个错误来了解更多关于使用 `Mutex<T>以及Rust "
"如何帮助我们正确使用它。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:140 src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:227
#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:328
msgid "\"Result: {}\""
msgstr "\"结果: {}\""

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:146
msgid ""
"We create a `counter` variable to hold an `i32` inside a `Mutex<T>`, as we "
"did in Listing 16-12. Next, we create 10 threads by iterating over a range "
"of numbers. We use `thread::spawn` and give all the threads the same "
"closure: one that moves the counter into the thread, acquires a lock on the "
"`Mutex<T>` by calling the `lock` method, and then adds 1 to the value in the "
"mutex. When a thread finishes running its closure, `num` will go out of "
"scope and release the lock so that another thread can acquire it."
msgstr ""
"我们创建一个 \"计数器\" 变量来将 `i32` 保存在一个 `Mutex<T>`中，就像我们在列"
"出16-12时所做的那样。 接下来，我们通过在一系列数字上的迭代来创建10条线程。 我"
"们使用 \"thread::spawn\" 并给所有线程相同的结束：将计数器移入线程， 调用 "
"`lock` 方法获得对 `Mutex<T>`的锁定，然后在mutex中添加一个 1。 当线程结束运行"
"关闭时，`num`将超出范围并释放锁，以便其他线程能够获得它。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:154
msgid ""
"In the main thread, we collect all the join handles. Then, as we did in "
"Listing 16-2, we call `join` on each handle to make sure all the threads "
"finish. At that point, the main thread will acquire the lock and print the "
"result of this program."
msgstr ""
"在主线程中，我们收集所有的加入句柄。 然后，正如我们在列举16-2时所做的那样，我"
"们在每个句柄上调用 `join` 来确保所有线程都已完成。 届时，主线程将获得锁并打印"
"此程序的结果。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:159
msgid "We hinted that this example wouldn’t compile. Now let’s find out why!"
msgstr "我们暗示这个示例不会编译。现在让我们知道为什么！"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:161
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo run\n"
"   Compiling shared-state v0.1.0 (file:///projects/shared-state)\n"
"error[E0382]: borrow of moved value: `counter`\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:21:29\n"
"   |\n"
" 5 |     let counter = Mutex::new(0);\n"
"   |         ------- move occurs because `counter` has type `std::sync::"
"Mutex<i32>`, which does not implement the `Copy` trait\n"
"...\n"
" 8 |     for _ in 0..10 {\n"
"   |     -------------- inside of this loop\n"
" 9 |         let handle = thread::spawn(move || {\n"
"   |                                    ------- value moved into closure "
"here, in previous iteration of loop\n"
"...\n"
"21 |     println!(\"Result: {}\", *counter.lock().unwrap());\n"
"   |                             ^^^^^^^ value borrowed here after move\n"
"   |\n"
"help: consider moving the expression out of the loop so it is only moved "
"once\n"
"   |\n"
" 8 ~     let mut value = counter.lock();\n"
" 9 ~     for _ in 0..10 {\n"
"10 |         let handle = thread::spawn(move || {\n"
"11 ~             let mut num = value.unwrap();\n"
"   |\n"
"\n"
"For more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0382`.\n"
"error: could not compile `shared-state` (bin \"shared-state\") due to 1 "
"previous error\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo run\n"
"   Compiling shared-state v0.1.0 (file:///projects/shared-state)\n"
"error[E0382]: borrow of moved value: `counter`\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:21:29\n"
"   |\n"
" 5 |     let counter = Mutex::new(0);\n"
"   |         ------- move occurs because `counter` has type `std::sync::"
"Mutex<i32>`, which does not implement the `Copy` trait\n"
"...\n"
" 8 |     for _ in 0..10 {\n"
"   |     -------------- inside of this loop\n"
" 9 |         let handle = thread::spawn(move || {\n"
"   |                                    ------- value moved into closure "
"here, in previous iteration of loop\n"
"...\n"
"21 |     println!(\"Result: {}\", *counter.lock().unwrap());\n"
"   |                             ^^^^^^^ value borrowed here after move\n"
"   |\n"
"help: consider moving the expression out of the loop so it is only moved "
"once\n"
"   |\n"
" 8 ~     let mut value = counter.lock();\n"
" 9 ~     for _ in 0..10 {\n"
"10 |         let handle = thread::spawn(move || {\n"
"11 ~             let mut num = value.unwrap();\n"
"   |\n"
"\n"
"For more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0382`.\n"
"error: could not compile `shared-state` (bin \"shared-state\") due to 1 "
"previous error\n"
"```"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:190
msgid ""
"The error message states that the `counter` value was moved in the previous "
"iteration of the loop. Rust is telling us that we can’t move the ownership "
"of lock `counter` into multiple threads. Let’s fix the compiler error with "
"the multiple-ownership method we discussed in Chapter 15."
msgstr ""
"错误消息表明，\"计数器\"是在循环的前一次迭代中移动的。 Rust 告诉我们，我们不"
"能将锁定计数器的所有权移动到多个线程中。 让我们修复编译器在第15章中讨论的多重"
"所有权方法的错误。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:195
msgid "Multiple Ownership with Multiple Threads"
msgstr "多个线程的多个所有权"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:197
msgid ""
"In Chapter 15, we gave a value to multiple owners by using the smart pointer "
"`Rc<T>` to create a reference-counted value. Let’s do the same here and see "
"what happens. We’ll wrap the `Mutex<T>` in `Rc<T>` in Listing 16-14 and "
"clone the `Rc<T>` before moving ownership to the thread."
msgstr ""
"在第15章中，我们通过使用智能指针`Rc<T>`来创建一个参考值计算给多个所有者。 让"
"我们在这里做同样的事情，看看发生了什么。 我们将把`Mutex<T>`在 `Rc<T>` 中包装"
"在列表16-14中，然后复制`Rc<T>`，然后将所有权移到线程。"

#: src/ch16-03-shared-state.md:233
msgid ""
"Once again, we compile and get... different errors! The compiler is teaching "
"us a lot:"
msgstr "我们再次编译并获取……不同的错误！编译者正在教我们很多："

