#: src/ch02-00-guessing-game-tutorial.md:1315
msgid ""
"This project was a hands-on way to introduce you to many new Rust concepts: "
"`let`, `match`, functions, the use of external crates, and more. In the next "
"few chapters, you’ll learn about these concepts in more detail. Chapter 3 "
"covers concepts that most programming languages have, such as variables, "
"data types, and functions, and shows how to use them in Rust. Chapter 4 "
"explores ownership, a feature that makes Rust different from other "
"languages. Chapter 5 discusses structs and method syntax, and Chapter 6 "
"explains how enums work."
msgstr ""
"这个项目是一种实践性的方式，旨在让您了解许多新的Rust概念：`let`、`match`、函"
"数、外部库的使用等等。在接下来的几章中，您将更详细地学习这些概念。第3章介绍了"
"大多数编程语言都有的概念，如变量、数据类型和函数，并展示了如何在Rust中使用它"
"们。第4章探讨了所有权这一特性，它使得Rust与其他语言有所不同。第5章……本文讨论"
"了结构体和方法语法，第6章则解释了枚举类型的工作原理。"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:1
msgid "Smart Pointers"
msgstr "智能指针"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:3
msgid ""
"A pointer is a general concept for a variable that contains an address in "
"memory. This address refers to, or “points at,” some other data. The most "
"common kind of pointer in Rust is a reference, which you learned about in "
"Chapter 4. References are indicated by the `&` symbol and borrow the value "
"they point to. They don’t have any special capabilities other than referring "
"to data, and they have no overhead."
msgstr ""
"指针是一种通用概念，指的是在内存中存储地址的变量。这个地址指向某个其他数据。"
"在Rust中，最常见的指针类型是引用，这一点你在第4章中已经了解过了。引用用`&`符"
"号表示，并且会借用它们所指向的值。除了指向数据之外，引用没有任何特殊功能，也"
"不会产生任何额外开销。"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:10
msgid ""
"_Smart pointers_, on the other hand, are data structures that act like a "
"pointer but also have additional metadata and capabilities. The concept of "
"smart pointers isn’t unique to Rust: Smart pointers originated in C++ and "
"exist in other languages as well. Rust has a variety of smart pointers "
"defined in the standard library that provide functionality beyond that "
"provided by references. To explore the general concept, we’ll look at a "
"couple of different examples of smart pointers, including a _reference "
"counting_ smart pointer type. This pointer enables you to allow data to have "
"multiple owners by keeping track of the number of owners and, when no owners "
"remain, cleaning up the data."
msgstr ""
"另一方面，智能指针是一种数据结构，它类似于普通指针，但还拥有额外的元数据和功"
"能。智能指针的概念并非Rust所独有：智能指针起源于C++，在其他语言中也有存在。"
"Rust的标准库中定义了多种智能指针，这些智能指针提供了超出普通引用所能提供的功"
"能。为了了解这一概念，我们将通过几个不同的例子来加以说明。智能指针，包括一种_"
"引用计数_智能指针类型。这种指针允许数据拥有多个所有者，通过跟踪所有者的数量来"
"实现；当没有所有者时，系统会清理该数据。"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:20
msgid ""
"In Rust, with its concept of ownership and borrowing, there is an additional "
"difference between references and smart pointers: While references only "
"borrow data, in many cases smart pointers _own_ the data they point to."
msgstr ""
"在Rust中，由于其所有权和借用概念的存在，引用和智能指针之间还有另一个区别：虽"
"然引用只是借用数据，但在许多情况下，智能指针实际上拥有它们所指向的数据。"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:24
msgid ""
"Smart pointers are usually implemented using structs. Unlike an ordinary "
"struct, smart pointers implement the `Deref` and `Drop` traits. The `Deref` "
"trait allows an instance of the smart pointer struct to behave like a "
"reference so that you can write your code to work with either references or "
"smart pointers. The `Drop` trait allows you to customize the code that’s run "
"when an instance of the smart pointer goes out of scope. In this chapter, "
"we’ll discuss both of these traits and demonstrate why they’re important to "
"smart pointers."
msgstr ""
"智能指针通常是通过结构体来实现的。与普通结构体不同，智能指针实现了`Deref`和"
"`Drop`这两个特性。`Deref`特性使得智能指针结构体的实例可以像引用一样使用，这样"
"你就可以编写代码来使用引用或智能指针。`Drop`特性则允许你自定义当智能指针的实"
"例超出作用域时执行的代码。在本章中，我们将讨论这些内容。这两种特性都体现了为"
"什么智能指针如此重要。"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:32
msgid ""
"Given that the smart pointer pattern is a general design pattern used "
"frequently in Rust, this chapter won’t cover every existing smart pointer. "
"Many libraries have their own smart pointers, and you can even write your "
"own. We’ll cover the most common smart pointers in the standard library:"
msgstr ""
"鉴于智能指针模式是Rust中常用的一种设计模式，本章不会涵盖所有现有的智能指针。"
"许多库都有自己的智能指针，甚至你可以自己编写智能指针。我们将介绍标准库中最为"
"常见的智能指针："

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:37
msgid "`Box<T>`, for allocating values on the heap"
msgstr "`Box<T>`，用于在堆上分配值"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:38
msgid "`Rc<T>`, a reference counting type that enables multiple ownership"
msgstr "`Rc<T>`，一种引用计数类型，能够实现多所有者共享"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:39
msgid ""
"`Ref<T>` and `RefMut<T>`, accessed through `RefCell<T>`, a type that "
"enforces the borrowing rules at runtime instead of compile time"
msgstr ""
"`Ref<T>`和`RefMut<T>`，通过`RefCell<T>`进行访问，这是一种在运行时而不是编译时"
"强制执行借用规则的机制"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:42
msgid ""
"In addition, we’ll cover the _interior mutability_ pattern where an "
"immutable type exposes an API for mutating an interior value. We’ll also "
"discuss reference cycles: how they can leak memory and how to prevent them."
msgstr ""
"此外，我们还将介绍“内部可变性”模式。在这种模式下，不可变类型会提供一个API来修"
"改内部值。我们还会讨论引用循环问题：它们如何导致内存泄漏以及如何防止这种情况"
"发生。"

#: src/ch15-00-smart-pointers.md:46
msgid "Let’s dive in!"
msgstr "让我们开始吧！"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:1
msgid "`Rc<T>`, the Reference-Counted Smart Pointer"
msgstr "`Rc<T>`，一种基于引用计数智能指针"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:3
msgid ""
"In the majority of cases, ownership is clear: You know exactly which "
"variable owns a given value. However, there are cases when a single value "
"might have multiple owners. For example, in graph data structures, multiple "
"edges might point to the same node, and that node is conceptually owned by "
"all of the edges that point to it. A node shouldn’t be cleaned up unless it "
"doesn’t have any edges pointing to it and so has no owners."
msgstr ""
"在大多数情况下，所有权是明确的：你确切知道哪个变量拥有某个特定值。 然而，在某"
"些情况下，单一价值可能有多个所有者。 例如，在图表数据结构中，多个边缘可能指向"
"同一个节点， 而且该节点在概念上为所有指向它的边缘所拥有。 节点不应被清理，除"
"非它没有任何边缘指向它，因此没有拥有者。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:10
msgid ""
"You have to enable multiple ownership explicitly by using the Rust type "
"`Rc<T>`, which is an abbreviation for _reference counting_. The `Rc<T>` type "
"keeps track of the number of references to a value to determine whether or "
"not the value is still in use. If there are zero references to a value, the "
"value can be cleaned up without any references becoming invalid."
msgstr ""
"您必须使用Rust type `Rc<T>`, 以明确方式启用多个所有权，这是_reference "
"counting_的缩写。 `Rc<T>`类型将跟踪一个值的引用数量，以确定该值是否仍在使"
"用。 如果一个值是零引用，则可以清理该值，而不会有任何引用变得无效。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:16
msgid ""
"Imagine `Rc<T>` as a TV in a family room. When one person enters to watch "
"TV, they turn it on. Others can come into the room and watch the TV. When "
"the last person leaves the room, they turn off the TV because it’s no longer "
"being used. If someone turns off the TV while others are still watching it, "
"there would be an uproar from the remaining TV watchers!"
msgstr ""
"想象一下`Rc<T>`作为家庭房间中的电视。 当一个人进入观看电视时，他们就把它关"
"掉。其他人可以进入房间观看电视。 当最后一个人离开房间时，他们会关闭电视，因为"
"它不再被使用。 如果有人在其他人仍在观看电视时关闭电视，就会有人从剩下的电视观"
"看器中拔掉！"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:22
msgid ""
"We use the `Rc<T>` type when we want to allocate some data on the heap for "
"multiple parts of our program to read and we can’t determine at compile time "
"which part will finish using the data last. If we knew which part would "
"finish last, we could just make that part the data’s owner, and the normal "
"ownership rules enforced at compile time would take effect."
msgstr ""
"当我们想要在堆上分配一些数据以便阅读我们程序的多个部分时，我们使用`Rc<T>`类"
"型。我们无法在编译时确定哪一部分将会用最后的数据来完成。 如果我们知道哪个部件"
"将最后完成，我们只能让这个部分成为数据的所有者， 而且在编纂时强制执行的正常所"
"有权规则将生效。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:28
msgid ""
"Note that `Rc<T>` is only for use in single-threaded scenarios. When we "
"discuss concurrency in Chapter 16, we’ll cover how to do reference counting "
"in multithreaded programs."
msgstr ""
"请注意，`Rc<T>`仅用于单线程场景。 当我们在第16章中讨论同义词时，我们将讨论如"
"何在多线程程序中进行参考计算。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:34
msgid "<a id=\"using-rct-to-share-data\"></a>"
msgstr "<a id=\"using-rct-to-share-data\"></a>"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:36
msgid "Sharing Data"
msgstr "共享数据"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:38
msgid ""
"Let’s return to our cons list example in Listing 15-5. Recall that we "
"defined it using `Box<T>`. This time, we’ll create two lists that both share "
"ownership of a third list. Conceptually, this looks similar to Figure 15-3."
msgstr ""
"让我们回到列举15-5列表中的我们的cons list 示例。回顾我们使用`Box<T>`来定义"
"它。 这一次，我们将创建两个列表，这两个列表都共享第三个列表的所有权。从概念上"
"来说，这似乎与图15-3相似。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:42
msgid ""
"<img alt=\"A linked list with the label 'a' pointing to three elements. The "
"first element contains the integer 5 and points to the second element. Th\n"
"e second element contains the integer 10 and points to the third element. "
"The third element contains the value 'Nil' that signifies the end of the l\n"
"ist; it does not point anywhere. A linked list with the label 'b' points to "
"an element that contains the integer 3 and points to the first element o\n"
"f list 'a'. A linked list with the label 'c' points to an element that "
"contains the integer 4 and also points to the first element of list 'a' so "
"th\n"
"at the tails of lists 'b' and 'c' are both list 'a'.\" src=\"img/trpl15-03."
"svg\" class=\"center\" />"
msgstr ""
"<img alt=\"A linked list with the label 'a' pointing to three elements. The "
"first element contains the integer 5 and points to the second element. Th\n"
"e second element contains the integer 10 and points to the third element. "
"The third element contains the value 'Nil' that signifies the end of the l\n"
"ist; it does not point anywhere. A linked list with the label 'b' points to "
"an element that contains the integer 3 and points to the first element o\n"
"f list 'a'. A linked list with the label 'c' points to an element that "
"contains the integer 4 and also points to the first element of list 'a' so "
"th\n"
"at the tails of lists 'b' and 'c' are both list 'a'.\" src=\"img/trpl15-03."
"svg\" class=\"center\" />"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:48
msgid ""
"<span class=\"caption\">Figure 15-3: Two lists, `b` and `c`, sharing "
"ownership of a third list, `a`</span>"
msgstr ""
"<span class=\"caption\">图15-3：两个列表, `b` 和 `c`, 共享第三个列表, `a`</"
"span>"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:51
msgid ""
"We’ll create list `a` that contains `5` and then `10`. Then, we’ll make two "
"more lists: `b` that starts with `3` and `c` that starts with `4`. Both the "
"`b` and `c` lists will then continue on to the first `a` list containing `5` "
"and `10`. In other words, both lists will share the first list containing "
"`5` and `10`."
msgstr ""
"我们将创建包含 `5` 和 `10` 的列表 `a` 。 然后，我们会再编制两个列表：`b`，开"
"头为`3`和`c`，开头为`4`。 然后，`b` 和 `c` 两种列表都将继续列在包含`5` 和 "
"`10`的第一个`a`列表中。 换句话说，这两个清单将共享第一个包含`5`和`10`的列表。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:57
msgid ""
"Trying to implement this scenario using our definition of `List` with "
"`Box<T>` won’t work, as shown in Listing 15-17."
msgstr ""
"尝试使用我们的 `list` 定义使用 `Box<T>` 来实现这个场景将无法工作，正如在上架"
"15-17 中所示。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:79
msgid "When we compile this code, we get this error:"
msgstr "当我们尝试编译这段代码时，会遇到这个错误："

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:81
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo run\n"
"   Compiling cons-list v0.1.0 (file:///projects/cons-list)\n"
"error[E0382]: use of moved value: `a`\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:11:30\n"
"   |\n"
" 9 |     let a = Cons(5, Box::new(Cons(10, Box::new(Nil))));\n"
"   |         - move occurs because `a` has type `List`, which does not "
"implement the `Copy` trait\n"
"10 |     let b = Cons(3, Box::new(a));\n"
"   |                              - value moved here\n"
"11 |     let c = Cons(4, Box::new(a));\n"
"   |                              ^ value used here after move\n"
"   |\n"
"note: if `List` implemented `Clone`, you could clone the value\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:1:1\n"
"   |\n"
" 1 | enum List {\n"
"   | ^^^^^^^^^ consider implementing `Clone` for this type\n"
"...\n"
"10 |     let b = Cons(3, Box::new(a));\n"
"   |                              - you could clone this value\n"
"\n"
"For more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0382`.\n"
"error: could not compile `cons-list` (bin \"cons-list\") due to 1 previous "
"error\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo run\n"
"   Compiling cons-list v0.1.0 (file:///projects/cons-list)\n"
"error[E0382]: use of moved value: `a`\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:11:30\n"
"   |\n"
" 9 |     let a = Cons(5, Box::new(Cons(10, Box::new(Nil))));\n"
"   |         - move occurs because `a` has type `List`, which does not "
"implement the `Copy` trait\n"
"10 |     let b = Cons(3, Box::new(a));\n"
"   |                              - value moved here\n"
"11 |     let c = Cons(4, Box::new(a));\n"
"   |                              ^ value used here after move\n"
"   |\n"
"note: if `List` implemented `Clone`, you could clone the value\n"
"  --> src/main.rs:1:1\n"
"   |\n"
" 1 | enum List {\n"
"   | ^^^^^^^^^ consider implementing `Clone` for this type\n"
"...\n"
"10 |     let b = Cons(3, Box::new(a));\n"
"   |                              - you could clone this value\n"
"\n"
"For more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0382`.\n"
"error: could not compile `cons-list` (bin \"cons-list\") due to 1 previous "
"error\n"
"```"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:107
msgid ""
"The `Cons` variants own the data they hold, so when we create the `b` list, "
"`a` is moved into `b` and `b` owns `a`. Then, when we try to use `a` again "
"when creating `c`, we’re not allowed to because `a` has been moved."
msgstr ""
"`一致性`变量拥有他们拥有的数据，所以当我们创建`b`列表时，`a`被移动到`b`和`b`"
"拥有`a`时。 然后，当我们尝试在创建 `c`时再次使用 `a`时，我们不允许使用 `a`。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:111
msgid ""
"We could change the definition of `Cons` to hold references instead, but "
"then we would have to specify lifetime parameters. By specifying lifetime "
"parameters, we would be specifying that every element in the list will live "
"at least as long as the entire list. This is the case for the elements and "
"lists in Listing 15-17, but not in every scenario."
msgstr ""
"我们可以修改`一致性'的定义，代之以提及，但是我们必须指定终身参数。 通过指明生"
"命周期参数，我们将指明清单中的每个元素至少与整个清单一样有效。 清单15至17所列"
"内容和清单的情况就是如此，但并非在每一种情况下。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:117
msgid ""
"Instead, we’ll change our definition of `List` to use `Rc<T>` in place of "
"`Box<T>`, as shown in Listing 15-18. Each `Cons` variant will now hold a "
"value and an `Rc<T>` pointing to a `List`. When we create `b`, instead of "
"taking ownership of `a`, we’ll clone the `Rc<List>` that `a` is holding, "
"thereby increasing the number of references from one to two and letting `a` "
"and `b` share ownership of the data in that `Rc<List>`. We’ll also clone `a` "
"when creating `c`, increasing the number of references from two to three. "
"Every time we call `Rc::clone`, the reference count to the data within the "
"`Rc<List>` will increase, and the data won’t be cleaned up unless there are "
"zero references to it."
msgstr ""
"相反，我们将更改“List”的定义，使用“Rc<T>”代替“Box<T>，如清单15-18所示。每"
"个“Cons”变量现在都将保存一个值和一个指向“List”的“Rc<T>”。当我们创建“b”时，我"
"们将克隆“a”所持有的“Rc<List>”，而不是拥有“a”的所有权，从而将引用的数量从一个"
"增加到两个，并让“a”和“b”共享“Rc<List>”中数据的所有权。在创建`c`时，我们还将克"
"隆`a`，将引用数量从两个增加到三个。每次我们调用`Rc:：clone`时，对`Rc<List>中"
"数据的引用计数都会增加，除非没有引用，否则数据不会被清理。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:148
msgid ""
"We need to add a `use` statement to bring `Rc<T>` into scope because it’s "
"not in the prelude. In `main`, we create the list holding `5` and `10` and "
"store it in a new `Rc<List>` in `a`. Then, when we create `b` and `c`, we "
"call the `Rc::clone` function and pass a reference to the `Rc<List>` in `a` "
"as an argument."
msgstr ""
"我们需要添加一条 `use` 语句，以便将 `Rc<T>` 纳入范围，因为它不在前文中。在 "
"`main` 中，我们创建了一个包含 `5` 和 `10` 的列表，并将其存储在一个新的 "
"`Rc<List>` 中，该 `Rc<List>` 又位于 `a` 中。然后，当我们创建 `b` 和 `c` 时，"
"我们调用 `Rc::clone` 函数，并将 `Rc<List>` 的引用作为参数传递给 `a`。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:154
msgid ""
"We could have called `a.clone()` rather than `Rc::clone(&a)`, but Rust’s "
"convention is to use `Rc::clone` in this case. The implementation of `Rc::"
"clone` doesn’t make a deep copy of all the data like most types’ "
"implementations of `clone` do. The call to `Rc::clone` only increments the "
"reference count, which doesn’t take much time. Deep copies of data can take "
"a lot of time. By using `Rc::clone` for reference counting, we can visually "
"distinguish between the deep-copy kinds of clones and the kinds of clones "
"that increase the reference count. When looking for performance problems in "
"the code, we only need to consider the deep-copy clones and can disregard "
"calls to `Rc::clone`."
msgstr ""
"我们本可以将 `a.clone()` 作为替代，而不是 `Rc::clone(&a)`。不过，Rust 的惯例"
"是在这种情况下使用 `Rc::clone`。`Rc::clone` 的实现并不会像大多数类型对 "
"`clone` 的实现那样，对所有数据进行深度复制。对 `Rc::clone` 的调用只会增加引用"
"计数，这个过程并不需要花费太多时间。而深度复制数据则可能需要很长时间。通过使"
"用 `Rc::clone` 来进行引用计数，我们可以直观地区分出那些需要深度复制的克隆对"
"象，以及那些只是增加引用计数的克隆对象。在查找代码中的性能问题时，我们只需要"
"考虑那些需要深度复制的克隆对象，而可以忽略对 `Rc::clone` 的调用。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:167
msgid "<a id=\"cloning-an-rct-increases-the-reference-count\"></a>"
msgstr "<a id=\"cloning-an-rct-increases-the-reference-count\"></a>"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:169
msgid "Cloning to Increase the Reference Count"
msgstr "克隆操作以增加引用计数"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:171
msgid ""
"Let’s change our working example in Listing 15-18 so that we can see the "
"reference counts changing as we create and drop references to the `Rc<List>` "
"in `a`."
msgstr ""
"让我们修改 Listing 15-18 中的示例，这样我们就可以看到在创建和删除对 "
"`Rc<List>` 的引用时，reference 计数是如何变化的。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:175
msgid ""
"In Listing 15-19, we’ll change `main` so that it has an inner scope around "
"list `c`; then, we can see how the reference count changes when `c` goes out "
"of scope."
msgstr ""
"在 Listing 15-19 中，我们将修改 `main`，使其在 list 周围有一个内部作用域。然"
"后，我们可以观察到当 `c` 离开作用域时，引用计数会发生怎样的变化。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:194
msgid "\"count after creating a = {}\""
msgstr "\"count after creating a = {}\""

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:196
msgid "\"count after creating b = {}\""
msgstr "\"count after creating b = {}\""

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:199
msgid "\"count after creating c = {}\""
msgstr "\"count after creating c = {}\""

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:201
msgid "\"count after c goes out of scope = {}\""
msgstr "\"count after c goes out of scope = {}\""

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:207
msgid ""
"At each point in the program where the reference count changes, we print the "
"reference count, which we get by calling the `Rc::strong_count` function. "
"This function is named `strong_count` rather than `count` because the "
"`Rc<T>` type also has a `weak_count`; we’ll see what `weak_count` is used "
"for in [“Preventing Reference Cycles Using `Weak<T>`”](ch15-06-reference-"
"cycles.html#preventing-reference-cycles-turning-an-rct-into-a-weakt)<!-- "
"ignore -->."
msgstr ""
"在程序的每个引用计数发生变化的点，我们都会打印出引用计数的值。这个数值是通过"
"调用 `Rc::strong_count` 函数得到的。这个函数被命名为 `strong_count`，而不是 "
"`count`，因为 `Rc<T>` 类型也包含 `weak_count`；我们将在[“使用 `Weak<T>` 防止"
"引用循环”](ch15-06-reference-cycles.html#preventing-reference-cycles-turning-"
"an-rct-into-a-weakt)<!-- ignore -->中了解 `weak_count` 的用途。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:213
msgid "This code prints the following:"
msgstr "这段代码会输出以下内容："

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:215
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo run\n"
"   Compiling cons-list v0.1.0 (file:///projects/cons-list)\n"
"    Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 0.45s\n"
"     Running `target/debug/cons-list`\n"
"count after creating a = 1\n"
"count after creating b = 2\n"
"count after creating c = 3\n"
"count after c goes out of scope = 2\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo run\n"
"   Compiling cons-list v0.1.0 (file:///projects/cons-list)\n"
"    Finished `dev` profile [unoptimized + debuginfo] target(s) in 0.45s\n"
"     Running `target/debug/cons-list`\n"
"count after creating a = 1\n"
"count after creating b = 2\n"
"count after creating c = 3\n"
"count after c goes out of scope = 2\n"
"```"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:226
msgid ""
"We can see that the `Rc<List>` in `a` has an initial reference count of 1; "
"then, each time we call `clone`, the count goes up by 1. When `c` goes out "
"of scope, the count goes down by 1. We don’t have to call a function to "
"decrease the reference count like we have to call `Rc::clone` to increase "
"the reference count: The implementation of the `Drop` trait decreases the "
"reference count automatically when an `Rc<T>` value goes out of scope."
msgstr ""
"我们可以看到，在 `a` 中，`Rc<List>` 的初始引用计数为 1；然后，每次我们调用 "
"`clone` 时，引用计数会增加 1。当 `c` 超出作用域时，引用计数会减少 1。我们不需"
"要像调用 `Rc::clone` 来增加引用计数那样，来调用函数来减少引用计数：`Drop`  "
"trait 的实现会在 `Rc<T>` 的值超出作用域时，自动减少引用计数。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:233
msgid ""
"What we can’t see in this example is that when `b` and then `a` go out of "
"scope at the end of `main`, the count is 0, and the `Rc<List>` is cleaned up "
"completely. Using `Rc<T>` allows a single value to have multiple owners, and "
"the count ensures that the value remains valid as long as any of the owners "
"still exist."
msgstr ""
"在这个例子中，我们无法看到的是，当 `b` 和 `a` 在 `main` 结束时退出作用域时，"
"计数变为0，而 `Rc<List>` 则被完全清理。使用 `Rc<T>` 则允许一个值拥有多个所有"
"者，而计数则确保该值在任何一个所有者仍然存在的情况下仍然有效。"

#: src/ch15-04-rc.md:239
msgid ""
"Via immutable references, `Rc<T>` allows you to share data between multiple "
"parts of your program for reading only. If `Rc<T>` allowed you to have "
"multiple mutable references too, you might violate one of the borrowing "
"rules discussed in Chapter 4: Multiple mutable borrows to the same place can "
"cause data races and inconsistencies. But being able to mutate data is very "
"useful! In the next section, we’ll discuss the interior mutability pattern "
"and the `RefCell<T>` type that you can use in conjunction with an `Rc<T>` to "
"work with this immutability restriction."
msgstr ""
"通过不可变引用，`Rc<T>`允许你在程序的多个部分之间仅进行数据读取。如果`Rc<T>`"
"也允许使用多个可变引用，那么可能会违反第4章中讨论的借用规则之一：对同一位置进"
"行多次可变借用会导致数据竞争和不一致性。不过，能够修改数据是非常有用的！在下"
"一节中，我们将讨论内部可变性模式，以及你可以与`Rc<T>`结合使用的`RefCell<T>`类"
"型，以配合这种不可变性限制来工作。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:1
msgid "`RefCell<T>` and the Interior Mutability Pattern"
msgstr "`RefCell<T>`与内部可变性模式"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:3
msgid ""
"_Interior mutability_ is a design pattern in Rust that allows you to mutate "
"data even when there are immutable references to that data; normally, this "
"action is disallowed by the borrowing rules. To mutate data, the pattern "
"uses `unsafe` code inside a data structure to bend Rust’s usual rules that "
"govern mutation and borrowing. Unsafe code indicates to the compiler that "
"we’re checking the rules manually instead of relying on the compiler to "
"check them for us; we will discuss unsafe code more in Chapter 20."
msgstr ""
"“内部可变性”是Rust中的一种设计模式，它允许你在存在不可变引用的情况下修改数"
"据。通常情况下，这种操作是被借用规则所禁止的。为了实现数据修改，该模式会在数"
"据结构内部使用`unsafe`代码，从而打破Rust中关于变异和借用的一般规则。使用"
"Unsafe代码可以向编译器表明，我们是手动检查这些规则，而不是依赖编译器来为我们"
"进行检查。我们将在第20章中更详细地讨论不安全的代码。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:11
msgid ""
"We can use types that use the interior mutability pattern only when we can "
"ensure that the borrowing rules will be followed at runtime, even though the "
"compiler can’t guarantee that. The `unsafe` code involved is then wrapped in "
"a safe API, and the outer type is still immutable."
msgstr ""
"我们只能在能够确保借用规则在运行时得到遵守的情况下，使用采用内部可变性模式的"
"类型。尽管编译器无法保证这一点，但涉及的``unsafe``代码会被封装在一个安全的API"
"中，而外部类型仍然保持不可变性。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:16
msgid ""
"Let’s explore this concept by looking at the `RefCell<T>` type that follows "
"the interior mutability pattern."
msgstr "让我们通过查看遵循内部可变性模式的`RefCell<T>`类型来探讨这个概念。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:21
msgid "<a id=\"enforcing-borrowing-rules-at-runtime-with-refcellt\"></a>"
msgstr "<a id=\"enforcing-borrowing-rules-at-runtime-with-refcellt\"></a>"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:23
msgid "Enforcing Borrowing Rules at Runtime"
msgstr "在运行时强制执行借用规则"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:25
msgid ""
"Unlike `Rc<T>`, the `RefCell<T>` type represents single ownership over the "
"data it holds. So, what makes `RefCell<T>` different from a type like "
"`Box<T>`? Recall the borrowing rules you learned in Chapter 4:"
msgstr ""
"与`Rc<T>`不同，`RefCell<T>`类型代表了对数据的单一所有权。那么，是什么让"
"`RefCell<T>`与`Box<T>`这样的类型有所不同呢？请回想一下你在第4章中学到的借用规"
"则："

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:29
msgid ""
"At any given time, you can have _either_ one mutable reference or any number "
"of immutable references (but not both)."
msgstr ""
"在任何时候，你可以拥有一个可变引用，或者任意数量的不变引用（但不能同时拥有两"
"者）。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:31
msgid "References must always be valid."
msgstr "引用必须始终有效。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:33
msgid ""
"With references and `Box<T>`, the borrowing rules’ invariants are enforced "
"at compile time. With `RefCell<T>`, these invariants are enforced _at "
"runtime_. With references, if you break these rules, you’ll get a compiler "
"error. With `RefCell<T>`, if you break these rules, your program will panic "
"and exit."
msgstr ""
"通过引用和`Box<T>`，借用规则的不变量在编译时就被强制执行了。而通过"
"`RefCell<T>`，这些不变量则在运行时被强制执行。使用引用方式时，如果你违反了这"
"些规则，将会出现编译器错误。而使用`RefCell<T>`时，如果你违反了这些规则，程序"
"将会崩溃并退出。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:38
msgid ""
"The advantages of checking the borrowing rules at compile time are that "
"errors will be caught sooner in the development process, and there is no "
"impact on runtime performance because all the analysis is completed "
"beforehand. For those reasons, checking the borrowing rules at compile time "
"is the best choice in the majority of cases, which is why this is Rust’s "
"default."
msgstr ""
"在编译时检查借用规则的优势在于，可以在开发过程中更早地发现错误，而且由于所有"
"分析都在事先完成，因此不会影响到运行时的性能。基于这些原因，在大多数情况下，"
"编译时检查借用规则是最佳选择，这也是Rust的默认行为。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:44
msgid ""
"The advantage of checking the borrowing rules at runtime instead is that "
"certain memory-safe scenarios are then allowed, where they would’ve been "
"disallowed by the compile-time checks. Static analysis, like the Rust "
"compiler, is inherently conservative. Some properties of code are impossible "
"to detect by analyzing the code: The most famous example is the Halting "
"Problem, which is beyond the scope of this book but is an interesting topic "
"to research."
msgstr ""
"在运行时检查借用规则的优势在于，某些内存安全的场景可以被允许，而这些场景在编"
"译时检查中是不被允许的。静态分析，比如Rust编译器，本质上是一种保守的方法。有"
"些代码特性是无法通过分析代码来检测的：最著名的例子就是停机问题，这个问题超出"
"了本书的讨论范围，但确实是一个值得研究的话题。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:51
msgid ""
"Because some analysis is impossible, if the Rust compiler can’t be sure the "
"code complies with the ownership rules, it might reject a correct program; "
"in this way, it’s conservative. If Rust accepted an incorrect program, users "
"wouldn’t be able to trust the guarantees Rust makes. However, if Rust "
"rejects a correct program, the programmer will be inconvenienced, but "
"nothing catastrophic can occur. The `RefCell<T>` type is useful when you’re "
"sure your code follows the borrowing rules but the compiler is unable to "
"understand and guarantee that."
msgstr ""
"因为有些分析是不可能的，如果Rust编译器无法确定代码是否符合所有权规则，它可能"
"会拒绝一个正确的程序。这样一来，Rust的做法就显得比较保守。如果Rust接受一个错"
"误的程序，用户就无法相信Rust所做出的保证。然而，如果Rust拒绝一个正确的程序，"
"程序员会感到不便，但并不会发生什么灾难性的情况。当您确信``RefCell<T>``类型"
"时，它非常有用。代码遵循了借用规则，但编译器无法理解和保证这一点。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:60
msgid ""
"Similar to `Rc<T>`, `RefCell<T>` is only for use in single-threaded "
"scenarios and will give you a compile-time error if you try using it in a "
"multithreaded context. We’ll talk about how to get the functionality of "
"`RefCell<T>` in a multithreaded program in Chapter 16."
msgstr ""
"类似于“<T>Rc”，“RefCell<T>”仅适用于单线程场景，如果你尝试在多线程环境中使用，"
"会给你编译时错误。我们将在<T>第 16 章讨论如何在多线程程序中实现“RefCell”的功"
"能。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:65
msgid ""
"Here is a recap of the reasons to choose `Box<T>`, `Rc<T>`, or `RefCell<T>`:"
msgstr "以下是选择`Box<T>`、`Rc<T>`或`RefCell<T>`的理由总结："

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:67
msgid ""
"`Rc<T>` enables multiple owners of the same data; `Box<T>` and `RefCell<T>` "
"have single owners."
msgstr ""
"`Rc<T>`支持同一数据由多个所有者管理；`Box<T>`和`RefCell<T>`则只有单个所有者。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:69
msgid ""
"`Box<T>` allows immutable or mutable borrows checked at compile time; "
"`Rc<T>` allows only immutable borrows checked at compile time; `RefCell<T>` "
"allows immutable or mutable borrows checked at runtime."
msgstr ""
"`Box<T>`允许在编译时检查可变或不可变的借用行为；`Rc<T>`仅允许在编译时检查不可"
"变的借用行为；`RefCell<T>`允许在运行时检查可变或不可变的借用行为。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:72
msgid ""
"Because `RefCell<T>` allows mutable borrows checked at runtime, you can "
"mutate the value inside the `RefCell<T>` even when the `RefCell<T>` is "
"immutable."
msgstr ""
"因为“RefCell<T>”允许在运行时检查可变借用，即使 <T>“RefCell<T>”是不可变的，也"
"可以在“RefCell”内部变异。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:76
msgid ""
"Mutating the value inside an immutable value is the interior mutability "
"pattern. Let’s look at a situation in which interior mutability is useful "
"and examine how it’s possible."
msgstr ""
"在不可变值内部修改其值是内部可变性模式。让我们来看一个内部可变性有用的场景，"
"并探讨如何实现这种特性。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:82
msgid ""
"<a id=\"interior-mutability-a-mutable-borrow-to-an-immutable-value\"></a>"
msgstr ""
"<a id=\"interior-mutability-a-mutable-borrow-to-an-immutable-value\"></a>"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:84
msgid "Using Interior Mutability"
msgstr "使用内部可变性"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:86
msgid ""
"A consequence of the borrowing rules is that when you have an immutable "
"value, you can’t borrow it mutably. For example, this code won’t compile:"
msgstr ""
"借用规则的一个结果是，当你有一个不可变的值时，你不能对其进行可变借用。例如，"
"这段代码将无法编译："

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:96
msgid "If you tried to compile this code, you’d get the following error:"
msgstr "如果你尝试编译这段代码，将会出现以下错误："

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:98
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo run\n"
"   Compiling borrowing v0.1.0 (file:///projects/borrowing)\n"
"error[E0596]: cannot borrow `x` as mutable, as it is not declared as "
"mutable\n"
" --> src/main.rs:3:13\n"
"  |\n"
"3 |     let y = &mut x;\n"
"  |             ^^^^^^ cannot borrow as mutable\n"
"  |\n"
"help: consider changing this to be mutable\n"
"  |\n"
"2 |     let mut x = 5;\n"
"  |         +++\n"
"\n"
"For more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0596`.\n"
"error: could not compile `borrowing` (bin \"borrowing\") due to 1 previous "
"error\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```console\n"
"$ cargo run\n"
"   Compiling borrowing v0.1.0 (file:///projects/borrowing)\n"
"error[E0596]: cannot borrow `x` as mutable, as it is not declared as "
"mutable\n"
" --> src/main.rs:3:13\n"
"  |\n"
"3 |     let y = &mut x;\n"
"  |             ^^^^^^ cannot borrow as mutable\n"
"  |\n"
"help: consider changing this to be mutable\n"
"  |\n"
"2 |     let mut x = 5;\n"
"  |         +++\n"
"\n"
"For more information about this error, try `rustc --explain E0596`.\n"
"error: could not compile `borrowing` (bin \"borrowing\") due to 1 previous "
"error\n"
"```"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:116
msgid ""
"However, there are situations in which it would be useful for a value to "
"mutate itself in its methods but appear immutable to other code. Code "
"outside the value’s methods would not be able to mutate the value. Using "
"`RefCell<T>` is one way to get the ability to have interior mutability, but "
"`RefCell<T>` doesn’t get around the borrowing rules completely: The borrow "
"checker in the compiler allows this interior mutability, and the borrowing "
"rules are checked at runtime instead. If you violate the rules, you’ll get a "
"`panic!` instead of a compiler error."
msgstr ""
"然而，在某些情况下，让一个值在自身的方法中发生变异，但对其他代码来说却看起来"
"是不可变的，这是非常有用的。位于该值方法之外的代码将无法对该值进行变异。使用"
"`RefCell<T>`是一种实现内部可变异性的方法，但`RefCell<T>`并不能完全解决借用问"
"题：编译器的借用检查器允许这种内部可变性，而借用规则仍然需要被检查。改为在运"
"行时进行。如果你违反了规则，你将收到一个`panic!`的提示，而不是编译器错误。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:125
msgid ""
"Let’s work through a practical example where we can use `RefCell<T>` to "
"mutate an immutable value and see why that is useful."
msgstr ""
"让我们通过一个实际例子来演示如何使用 ``RefCell<T>`` 来修改一个不可变的值，并"
"了解为什么这样做是有用的。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:130
msgid "<a id=\"a-use-case-for-interior-mutability-mock-objects\"></a>"
msgstr "<a id=\"a-use-case-for-interior-mutability-mock-objects\"></a>"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:132
msgid "Testing with Mock Objects"
msgstr "使用模拟对象进行测试"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:134
msgid ""
"Sometimes during testing a programmer will use a type in place of another "
"type, in order to observe particular behavior and assert that it’s "
"implemented correctly. This placeholder type is called a _test double_. "
"Think of it in the sense of a stunt double in filmmaking, where a person "
"steps in and substitutes for an actor to do a particularly tricky scene. "
"Test doubles stand in for other types when we’re running tests. _Mock "
"objects_ are specific types of test doubles that record what happens during "
"a test so that you can assert that the correct actions took place."
msgstr ""
"在测试过程中，有时程序员会使用一种类型来代替另一种类型，以便观察特定的行为，"
"并确认该类型是否正确实现。这种占位符类型被称为“测试用双精度型”。可以将其想象"
"成电影中的替身演员，他们代替真实的演员来表演特别复杂的场景。当我们进行测试"
"时，测试用双精度型就代表了其他类型。而“模拟对象”则是特定类型的测试工具。该记"
"录详细描述了测试过程中的所有事件，以便您可以确认正确的操作确实已经执行了。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:143
msgid ""
"Rust doesn’t have objects in the same sense as other languages have objects, "
"and Rust doesn’t have mock object functionality built into the standard "
"library as some other languages do. However, you can definitely create a "
"struct that will serve the same purposes as a mock object."
msgstr ""
"Rust中的对象与其他语言中的对象有所不同，而且Rust的标准库中没有内置类似于其他"
"语言中的模拟对象功能。不过，您完全可以创建一个结构体，使其具备与模拟对象相同"
"的功能。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:148
msgid ""
"Here’s the scenario we’ll test: We’ll create a library that tracks a value "
"against a maximum value and sends messages based on how close to the maximum "
"value the current value is. This library could be used to keep track of a "
"user’s quota for the number of API calls they’re allowed to make, for "
"example."
msgstr ""
"我们将测试以下场景：我们创建一个库，该库会跟踪一个数值，并根据当前数值与最大"
"值之间的差距来发送消息。例如，这个库可以用来记录用户允许的API调用次数配额。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:153
msgid ""
"Our library will only provide the functionality of tracking how close to the "
"maximum a value is and what the messages should be at what times. "
"Applications that use our library will be expected to provide the mechanism "
"for sending the messages: The application could show the message to the user "
"directly, send an email, send a text message, or do something else. The "
"library doesn’t need to know that detail. All it needs is something that "
"implements a trait we’ll provide, called `Messenger`. Listing 15-20 shows "
"the library code."
msgstr ""
"我们的库只会提供追踪某个值距离最大值还有多远的功能，以及在这些时间点应该发送"
"哪些消息。使用我们库的应用程序需要自行实现发送消息的机制：应用程序可以直接向"
"用户显示消息，或者发送电子邮件、发送短信，或者采取其他方式。库不需要了解这些"
"细节。它只需要一个实现了我们定义的特征的组件即可。提供的内容被命名为"
"`Messenger`。列表15-20展示了相关的库代码。"

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:192
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:255
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:387
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:511
msgid "\"Error: You are over your quota!\""
msgstr "\"错误：您超过了您的配额！\""

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:195
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:258
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:390
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:514
msgid "\"Urgent warning: You've used up over 90% of your quota!\""
msgstr "\"紧急警告：你已经占用了超过90%的配额！\""

#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:198
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:261
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:393
#: src/ch15-05-interior-mutability.md:517
